=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: router16
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** FRR routing daemon (ospfd) on router16 — the OSPF relay connecting Campus 1's multilayer switch to the WAN backbone.

**Mechanism:** router16 sits at the critical junction between mswitch0 (Campus 1 gateway, 10.2.2.1/24 via bond0) and backbone router7 (172.30.1.1/24 via eth2). When ospfd on router16 fails, neither adjacency forms: mswitch0 loses its only OSPF peer, and router7 loses the link to the Campus 1 domain. Without any learned routes, mswitch0's routing table is reduced to just its four locally-connected VLAN subnets (172.16.10/20/30.0/24 and 10.2.2.0/24). Any packet destined for Campus 2 or backbone addresses hits mswitch0 with no matching route, causing it to generate ICMP "Destination Net Unreachable" — which is exactly what pc5 and dc_pc5 received in live probes.

**Localization:** router16, FRR systemd service (`Active: failed`), ospfd process absent. Both physical uplink interfaces are UP — bond0 (eth0+eth1, 10.2.2.1/24) toward mswitch0 and eth2 (172.30.1.1/24) toward router7. The failure is daemon-level, not link-level. On mswitch0, the `br0` interface (10.2.2.2/24, OSPF area 0.0.0.0) is the uplink interface left with zero neighbors.

**Root cause:** The FRR service on router16 has crashed and entered a `failed` state, taking the ospfd process down with it, severing all OSPF adjacencies across the Campus 1 ↔ backbone path.

**Fix:** Restart the FRR service on router16 (`systemctl restart frr`), which will bring ospfd back up, re-establish the mswitch0↔router16 and router16↔router7 OSPF adjacencies, and restore full route distribution to Campus 1.
=== END ===